00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:14,740
(Watch on KonFlix.vip)

1
00:01:49,705 --> 00:01:51,305
LU'S SHOP

2
00:02:07,825 --> 00:02:10,385
LU'S SHOP

3
00:02:15,465 --> 00:02:16,745
You're Mr. Lu, right?

4
00:02:17,585 --> 00:02:18,425
Yes.

5
00:02:28,745 --> 00:02:31,105
This pair of shoes… I've seen them.

6
00:02:32,825 --> 00:02:34,905
Did someone ask you
to make these this summer?

7
00:02:34,985 --> 00:02:36,225
Who was that person?

8
00:02:36,905 --> 00:02:37,745
No idea.

9
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:40,745
My dad took that job.

10
00:02:40,825 --> 00:02:43,385
He's out of town getting materials.
Maybe in two days?

11
00:02:51,665 --> 00:02:55,145
Two days later,
that young officer showed up on time.

12
00:02:55,745 --> 00:02:56,625
He met my dad.

13
00:03:06,025 --> 00:03:06,865
That's right.

14
00:03:07,585 --> 00:03:10,465
Half a year ago, a young guy came to me.

15
00:03:10,545 --> 00:03:13,665
He insisted I turn
a perfectly good pair of red heels

16
00:03:13,745 --> 00:03:15,465
into blue ones.

17
00:03:15,545 --> 00:03:18,385
It just felt off,
so I didn't want the job.

18
00:03:19,385 --> 00:03:21,785
But then he offered me 800 yuan.

19
00:03:21,865 --> 00:03:23,465
Eight hundred yuan

20
00:03:23,545 --> 00:03:25,905
could buy several pairs
of brand-name shoes.

21
00:03:26,465 --> 00:03:29,345
A real pair of shoes,
he wanted it turned fake.

22
00:03:29,425 --> 00:03:31,585
What was he after?

23
00:03:32,585 --> 00:03:34,585
What did he look like? Do you remember?

24
00:03:36,585 --> 00:03:38,825
A guy in his thirties.

25
00:03:38,905 --> 00:03:40,025
Wearing sunglasses.

26
00:03:40,105 --> 00:03:42,505
His face… I didn't see clearly.

27
00:03:43,585 --> 00:03:44,625
How tall?

28
00:03:45,545 --> 00:03:46,545
His height…

29
00:03:48,025 --> 00:03:49,625
You, stand up.

30
00:03:53,145 --> 00:03:54,265
About my son's height.

31
00:03:54,345 --> 00:03:55,705
Around 175 cm.

32
00:03:55,785 --> 00:03:57,105
Short haircut.

33
00:03:57,185 --> 00:03:58,905
When he spoke, his voice was hoarse.

34
00:03:59,545 --> 00:04:01,625
He had three burn marks on his arm.

35
00:04:03,105 --> 00:04:03,945
Burn marks?

36
00:04:04,025 --> 00:04:05,865
Scars from being burned with cigarettes.

37
00:04:12,105 --> 00:04:14,385
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

38
00:04:14,465 --> 00:04:15,825
BLUE LEATHER HEELS, LILI

39
00:04:15,905 --> 00:04:17,545
DU MINGLIANG'S MOTHER, SHOE SELLER
LIU GUIFANG

40
00:04:17,624 --> 00:04:22,385
SHOEMAKER MR. LU
MAN WITH THREE BURN SCARS

41
00:04:22,465 --> 00:04:26,225
This man is key to solving
the Yuanlongli June 30th case.

42
00:04:26,945 --> 00:04:29,145
Very likely, he's the real killer.

43
00:04:30,105 --> 00:04:31,585
Same plan as always.

44
00:04:31,665 --> 00:04:32,785
We cover both ends.

45
00:04:32,865 --> 00:04:35,225
I'll stay in Yuanlongli.

46
00:04:35,305 --> 00:04:37,825
You go to the branch
and check local stations.

47
00:04:37,905 --> 00:04:40,705
Try to find any useful leads.

48
00:04:40,785 --> 00:04:42,425
This is like finding a needle
in a haystack.

49
00:04:42,505 --> 00:04:46,025
If we had fingerprints,
I could search the database.

50
00:04:46,105 --> 00:04:48,625
But those burn scars,
how do I even ask about that?

51
00:04:50,865 --> 00:04:54,185
I think Uncle Ran went through
the same thing back then.

52
00:04:54,785 --> 00:04:57,585
Otherwise, he would've caught
that guy already.

53
00:04:58,905 --> 00:05:00,825
Just… think it through again.

54
00:05:01,505 --> 00:05:04,705
If you were Uncle Ran,
where would you go next?

55
00:05:05,865 --> 00:05:07,745
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

56
00:05:20,385 --> 00:05:23,225
Han, it's me.

57
00:05:23,745 --> 00:05:24,585
Um…

58
00:05:26,785 --> 00:05:29,145
Hang on! Let me tell you in a second!

59
00:05:47,545 --> 00:05:48,545
My eyes are going blurry.

60
00:05:48,625 --> 00:05:51,825
No idea which idiot came up with this
just to mess with me.

61
00:05:55,865 --> 00:05:56,825
Uncle Ran,

62
00:05:57,865 --> 00:06:00,425
looking at all that stuff,
doesn't it annoy you?

63
00:06:01,065 --> 00:06:01,905
Of course.

64
00:06:02,585 --> 00:06:04,465
It's worse when you can't find clues.

65
00:06:05,345 --> 00:06:09,905
But I have a theory
that helps solve tough problems.

66
00:06:09,985 --> 00:06:10,785
Tell me!

67
00:06:15,225 --> 00:06:17,625
Look, when you're solving a problem,

68
00:06:17,705 --> 00:06:19,225
it's like untangling a ball of thread.

69
00:06:19,825 --> 00:06:21,265
You have to look closely

70
00:06:21,905 --> 00:06:22,945
and find the loose end.

71
00:06:24,105 --> 00:06:27,305
Once you find it, just pull,

72
00:06:28,145 --> 00:06:30,785
and the whole thing unravels.

73
00:06:31,825 --> 00:06:34,305
Right now, I'm looking for that end.

74
00:06:38,425 --> 00:06:40,385
The wind blew it away.

75
00:06:40,465 --> 00:06:42,265
Now it's even harder to find.

76
00:06:42,345 --> 00:06:44,825
That's weird. Why is it so windy today?

77
00:06:50,345 --> 00:06:51,545
Thanks.

78
00:07:00,705 --> 00:07:02,945
PHYSICAL EVIDENCE PHOTOS

79
00:07:21,785 --> 00:07:24,945
LIST OF EVIDENCE

80
00:07:26,505 --> 00:07:29,145
The key to this case… What is it?

81
00:07:31,025 --> 00:07:31,945
‎WHERE DID YOU HIDE THEM?

82
00:07:32,025 --> 00:07:33,105
‎I DIDN'T HIDE THEM. SIR, DID YOU CATCH ME
‎BECAUSE SOMETHING HAPPENED TO MENGMENG?

83
00:07:35,625 --> 00:07:37,585
Why so dumb?

84
00:07:40,545 --> 00:07:41,505
Who are you calling dumb?

85
00:07:44,065 --> 00:07:45,625
Me.

86
00:07:45,705 --> 00:07:47,625
There's been a loose thread here.

87
00:07:47,705 --> 00:07:49,545
How did I miss it?

88
00:07:49,625 --> 00:07:51,105
Q: DID YOU EVER GIFT XU MENG CLOTHING?
A: YES.

89
00:07:52,465 --> 00:07:54,985
Xiaohe, pass me the tape.

90
00:08:13,065 --> 00:08:15,665
PUBLIC SECURITY

91
00:08:17,425 --> 00:08:19,065
WEIYANG PUBLIC SECURITY
BUREAU NANSHAN BRANCH ARCHIVE ROOM

92
00:08:27,985 --> 00:08:29,305
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION FILES

93
00:08:33,585 --> 00:08:34,784
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION FILES

94
00:08:48,905 --> 00:08:51,025
Q: DID YOU EVER GIFT XU MENG CLOTHING?
A: YES.

95
00:08:56,945 --> 00:08:58,505
Q: ANY BOWLS DRESS?

96
00:08:58,585 --> 00:09:00,385
A: I MIGHT. I BOUGHT 11 DRESSES
ALL COME WITH DRY CLEANING GIFT CARD

97
00:09:00,465 --> 00:09:03,225
When we interrogated Sun Zhengyong,
I was there too.

98
00:09:03,745 --> 00:09:05,905
Sun Zhengyong had an alibi.

99
00:09:05,985 --> 00:09:08,385
<i>Qu Dahai can also testify for him.</i>

100
00:09:08,465 --> 00:09:10,385
<i>He's not related</i>
<i>to the Yuanlongli June 30th case.</i>

101
00:09:11,105 --> 00:09:14,745
And the Bowls dress
mentioned in the statement,

102
00:09:14,825 --> 00:09:18,225
Xiao Ran already checked the store's
sales records back then.

103
00:09:18,305 --> 00:09:19,625
Everything matched.

104
00:09:19,705 --> 00:09:21,905
<i>Are you sure</i>
<i>this is the loose thread he meant?</i>

105
00:09:21,985 --> 00:09:24,505
I saw Uncle Ran place the tape myself.

106
00:09:25,065 --> 00:09:27,025
Dad, try to think carefully again.

107
00:09:27,105 --> 00:09:29,265
<i>Back then, did Uncle Ran ever mention</i>

108
00:09:29,345 --> 00:09:32,225
<i>the Bowls dress or Sun Zhengyong?</i>

109
00:09:45,545 --> 00:09:46,665
We're back.

110
00:09:48,105 --> 00:09:50,705
BLESSING

111
00:09:53,745 --> 00:09:55,985
You didn't cause Uncle Ran
any trouble, right?

112
00:09:56,065 --> 00:09:57,705
Xiaohe was very well-behaved today.

113
00:09:58,225 --> 00:10:02,145
She even did great
and caught up on all her missed work.

114
00:10:02,825 --> 00:10:04,705
That's all thanks to Uncle Ran.
He taught me well.

115
00:10:04,785 --> 00:10:05,785
Unlike some people,

116
00:10:05,865 --> 00:10:07,025
ask them anything,

117
00:10:07,105 --> 00:10:09,025
they know nothing,
and just shake their head.

118
00:10:09,745 --> 00:10:11,985
Are you taking a jab at me?

119
00:10:12,825 --> 00:10:15,265
I get a question right sometimes, okay?

120
00:10:15,345 --> 00:10:17,225
If teachers taught like Uncle Ran,

121
00:10:17,305 --> 00:10:18,945
using that detective mindset,

122
00:10:19,025 --> 00:10:20,225
I would've graduated early.

123
00:10:21,065 --> 00:10:25,105
You, are you trying to graduate early
to go to Beijing for rock music?

124
00:10:25,705 --> 00:10:27,105
I could even become a cop on the side.

125
00:10:28,465 --> 00:10:30,185
What, on the side?

126
00:10:30,265 --> 00:10:32,585
You, put in the same effort
you use for rock music,

127
00:10:32,665 --> 00:10:35,585
you still wouldn't match
even half of your Uncle Ran's skills.

128
00:10:35,665 --> 00:10:37,065
Uncle Ran isn't a superhero.

129
00:10:37,145 --> 00:10:38,585
He can't even read sheet music.

130
00:10:40,465 --> 00:10:41,585
How about this?

131
00:10:41,665 --> 00:10:43,105
You teach me music notation,

132
00:10:43,185 --> 00:10:44,305
and I teach you criminal investigation.

133
00:10:44,385 --> 00:10:46,145
We learn from each other.

134
00:10:46,225 --> 00:10:47,345
Then who's the teacher?

135
00:10:48,225 --> 00:10:49,065
We both are.

136
00:10:50,305 --> 00:10:51,265
Deal.

137
00:10:52,065 --> 00:10:53,505
Deal.

138
00:10:53,585 --> 00:10:54,505
Rock on.

139
00:10:55,305 --> 00:10:56,145
And even threw up a rock sign?

140
00:10:56,225 --> 00:10:58,945
Hurry and go wash some fruit
for your teacher.

141
00:11:05,425 --> 00:11:07,945
Sir, your package.

142
00:11:10,305 --> 00:11:11,665
QI YUANSHAN

143
00:11:13,985 --> 00:11:15,425
This is the Mount Wu accident file.

144
00:11:16,025 --> 00:11:17,225
We don't need it now.

145
00:11:17,305 --> 00:11:18,265
Perfect timing.

146
00:11:18,345 --> 00:11:20,425
I just wrote something.
Take a look for me.

147
00:11:24,025 --> 00:11:26,265
DEADLY BUILDING CASE
YUANLONGLI JUNE 30TH MEMOIR

148
00:11:26,985 --> 00:11:28,745
This title, it's catchy.

149
00:11:29,945 --> 00:11:32,345
If this gets published,
the title alone will sell it out.

150
00:11:33,145 --> 00:11:35,105
Titles are just for show.

151
00:11:35,185 --> 00:11:36,425
I care more about the content.

152
00:11:40,745 --> 00:11:42,905
ON THE DAY OF JUNE 30TH, 1997…

153
00:11:46,185 --> 00:11:49,505
<i>Times change. Energy's limited.</i>
<i>Focus on the big stuff.</i>

154
00:11:50,105 --> 00:11:51,665
Start with clothes and food.

155
00:11:52,185 --> 00:11:54,025
I get the first three lines.

156
00:11:54,105 --> 00:11:56,025
What does the last one mean?

157
00:11:56,105 --> 00:11:57,305
It's simple.

158
00:11:57,985 --> 00:11:59,505
What can't we live without?

159
00:12:00,025 --> 00:12:01,505
Eating, drinking, and daily needs.

160
00:12:01,585 --> 00:12:03,585
Those things leave clues most easily.

161
00:12:05,825 --> 00:12:06,865
Sir.

162
00:12:07,745 --> 00:12:09,225
That's a great rule.

163
00:12:09,305 --> 00:12:10,625
Why cross it out?

164
00:12:11,545 --> 00:12:13,745
Those were just silly rhymes I made up.

165
00:12:13,825 --> 00:12:14,905
So much for being a top student.

166
00:12:14,985 --> 00:12:17,505
A few words from me fooled you
into calling me "Sir".

167
00:12:22,065 --> 00:12:23,665
Actually, the Yuanlongli June 30th case

168
00:12:23,745 --> 00:12:25,745
has two clothing-related clues.

169
00:12:26,665 --> 00:12:28,225
One is the blue heels.

170
00:12:29,825 --> 00:12:31,465
The other is the Bowls dress.

171
00:12:33,465 --> 00:12:34,305
Right, sir.

172
00:12:34,905 --> 00:12:37,105
Did you write
the Sun Zhengyong interrogation part?

173
00:12:38,545 --> 00:12:39,505
Not yet.

174
00:12:39,585 --> 00:12:40,985
I'm only at Song Qingsong.

175
00:12:41,065 --> 00:12:42,785
Sun Zhengyong, like Song Qingsong,

176
00:12:42,865 --> 00:12:44,585
later ran off
because of illegal fundraising

177
00:12:44,665 --> 00:12:45,665
and debt evasion.

178
00:12:46,625 --> 00:12:49,225
Are you also handling financial cases now?

179
00:12:49,305 --> 00:12:51,625
How did you get to Sun Zhengyong?

180
00:12:54,585 --> 00:12:57,665
Ran did mention Sun Zhengyong to me.

181
00:12:58,625 --> 00:12:59,945
Back then, Uncle Ran

182
00:13:00,025 --> 00:13:01,865
was holding a photo
before he mentioned the loose thread.

183
00:13:02,745 --> 00:13:06,825
<i>But what exactly was in the photo,</i>
<i>I don't know.</i>

184
00:13:07,865 --> 00:13:09,025
A photo.

185
00:13:09,905 --> 00:13:11,025
The loose thread.

186
00:13:12,665 --> 00:13:13,825
Sun Zhengyong.

187
00:13:17,985 --> 00:13:20,465
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

188
00:13:20,545 --> 00:13:23,545
Could it be the dress from Xu Meng's home?

189
00:13:24,145 --> 00:13:25,625
<i>Check it now.</i>

190
00:13:25,705 --> 00:13:28,305
<i>There should be a photo</i>
<i>of a dress in the files.</i>

191
00:13:28,385 --> 00:13:29,945
<i>It's a Bowls dress.</i>

192
00:13:30,985 --> 00:13:32,905
I've gone through
these two boxes a hundred times.

193
00:13:32,985 --> 00:13:34,865
There's no photo of a Bowls dress.

194
00:13:35,865 --> 00:13:37,945
Could it have been borrowed by Uncle Ran,

195
00:13:38,025 --> 00:13:39,745
<i>like those blue heels?</i>

196
00:13:41,065 --> 00:13:44,065
Ran must have compared the photo

197
00:13:44,785 --> 00:13:46,585
and found a problem in the statement.

198
00:13:46,665 --> 00:13:48,865
<i>Go there now. Go to the Bowls store.</i>

199
00:13:49,465 --> 00:13:51,465
Check Sun Zhengyong's purchase records.

200
00:13:59,985 --> 00:14:00,905
Hello.

201
00:14:00,985 --> 00:14:02,065
Hello.

202
00:14:02,985 --> 00:14:04,905
From Nanshan Branch.
I'm here to ask about something.

203
00:14:05,425 --> 00:14:06,825
Ask away, Officer.

204
00:14:09,545 --> 00:14:10,945
You're Jessica too?

205
00:14:11,025 --> 00:14:12,785
When I came five years ago,

206
00:14:12,865 --> 00:14:14,665
there was a male staff member
with the same name.

207
00:14:15,425 --> 00:14:17,345
Here, we change staff, not names.

208
00:14:19,465 --> 00:14:20,585
I wanted to ask.

209
00:14:21,545 --> 00:14:25,625
In 1997, did buying this dress
come with a dry-cleaning card?

210
00:14:25,705 --> 00:14:26,545
Yes.

211
00:14:26,625 --> 00:14:28,545
Not every style did.

212
00:14:28,625 --> 00:14:30,625
But this one is a Bowls classic.

213
00:14:30,705 --> 00:14:32,465
No matter what year you bought it,
it came with one.

214
00:14:32,545 --> 00:14:34,905
And it was a Bowls dry-cleaning card.

215
00:14:36,305 --> 00:14:37,345
Is this it?

216
00:14:38,105 --> 00:14:39,145
That's right. That's the one.

217
00:14:40,065 --> 00:14:43,385
Can you use this card
to find out who bought the dress?

218
00:14:44,705 --> 00:14:45,785
I'm afraid not.

219
00:14:45,865 --> 00:14:47,785
The dry-cleaning cards aren't numbered.

220
00:14:50,425 --> 00:14:51,545
One moment.

221
00:14:54,225 --> 00:14:56,665
This dress was once
brought in for dry cleaning.

222
00:14:56,745 --> 00:14:59,625
Look. Here. There's a check mark.

223
00:15:01,505 --> 00:15:02,425
If it was dry-cleaned,

224
00:15:02,505 --> 00:15:03,985
we can find the record.

225
00:15:04,065 --> 00:15:05,905
I can pull up all the dry-cleaning records

226
00:15:05,985 --> 00:15:08,225
for this dress from 1997.

227
00:15:08,305 --> 00:15:10,225
Dry-cleaning records
are linked to sales records.

228
00:15:10,825 --> 00:15:12,505
-Thank you so much.
-You're welcome.

229
00:15:16,225 --> 00:15:17,305
-Hello.
-Hello.

230
00:15:17,385 --> 00:15:18,625
Excuse me. How can I help you?

231
00:15:18,705 --> 00:15:20,945
I wanted to ask. This store,
how long has it been open?

232
00:15:21,985 --> 00:15:23,705
Our store is the Weiyang flagship store.

233
00:15:23,785 --> 00:15:24,785
It's been open for over 20 years.

234
00:15:27,425 --> 00:15:30,705
Then back in 2003,
did you see this person?

235
00:15:30,785 --> 00:15:31,905
2003?

236
00:15:32,425 --> 00:15:33,545
I was still in high school then.

237
00:15:37,065 --> 00:15:40,625
So, do you have sales records
for the 1997 classic dress?

238
00:15:41,265 --> 00:15:43,305
I'm sorry. Those are internal documents.

239
00:15:43,385 --> 00:15:44,585
We can't just show them.

240
00:15:45,625 --> 00:15:46,865
Police investigation.

241
00:15:46,945 --> 00:15:48,625
It's not that I won't help.

242
00:15:48,705 --> 00:15:51,705
Our store's sales records
are kept for five years at most.

243
00:15:52,225 --> 00:15:54,185
Back in 1997, they were still paper files.

244
00:15:54,265 --> 00:15:55,545
They were destroyed long ago.

245
00:15:57,745 --> 00:15:59,865
But the provincial headquarters
has an archive room.

246
00:15:59,945 --> 00:16:02,185
They should have digital backups.
You can ask there.

247
00:16:03,545 --> 00:16:05,025
Provincial headquarters.

248
00:16:05,105 --> 00:16:06,225
Thank you.

249
00:16:07,705 --> 00:16:09,745
Officer, I'm sorry.

250
00:16:09,825 --> 00:16:11,785
The 1997 records have all been archived.

251
00:16:11,865 --> 00:16:13,225
We need to apply to headquarters.

252
00:16:13,305 --> 00:16:15,225
It'll take about two or three days.

253
00:16:17,585 --> 00:16:18,425
Thanks, that'd be great.

254
00:16:18,505 --> 00:16:19,865
-I'll come back in two days.
-Okay.

255
00:16:19,945 --> 00:16:22,265
HUOFENG INSURANCE

256
00:16:44,265 --> 00:16:45,305
Qiao.

257
00:16:51,545 --> 00:16:53,425
Ran, why did you ask me
to dinner so suddenly?

258
00:16:53,505 --> 00:16:54,545
I wasn't even

259
00:16:55,625 --> 00:16:56,585
prepared.

260
00:16:57,625 --> 00:16:59,185
Why prepare for dinner?

261
00:17:00,025 --> 00:17:01,065
What do you want?

262
00:17:02,465 --> 00:17:03,745
Just some rice noodles is fine.

263
00:17:06,785 --> 00:17:09,105
You ordered braised ribs,
sweet-and-sour fish,

264
00:17:09,184 --> 00:17:12,145
boiled beef, and boiled shrimp,
mushrooms with greens, and egg soup.

265
00:17:12,224 --> 00:17:13,944
Six dishes total.
Would you like anything else?

266
00:17:14,025 --> 00:17:15,505
The shrimp,

267
00:17:16,585 --> 00:17:17,505
maybe skip it.

268
00:17:17,585 --> 00:17:18,625
That's all for now.

269
00:17:18,704 --> 00:17:21,184
-Please serve it quickly.
-Sure.

270
00:17:23,345 --> 00:17:25,905
You ordered too much.
It's expensive and wasteful.

271
00:17:26,585 --> 00:17:28,745
It's fine. We can take leftovers home.

272
00:17:37,185 --> 00:17:38,985
FILE

273
00:17:40,305 --> 00:17:44,025
I pulled this from the evidence room.

274
00:17:44,865 --> 00:17:46,585
After thinking it over,

275
00:17:48,065 --> 00:17:50,105
it's best to leave it with you.

276
00:18:00,665 --> 00:18:02,465
Don't open it yet.

277
00:18:04,825 --> 00:18:07,265
Then, when you tell me to open it,

278
00:18:07,345 --> 00:18:09,425
I'll open it then.

279
00:18:16,585 --> 00:18:17,945
FILE

280
00:18:27,865 --> 00:18:29,105
What's wrong?

281
00:18:29,185 --> 00:18:32,185
On New Year's Eve, what are your plans?

282
00:18:32,905 --> 00:18:34,385
Are you going home?

283
00:18:37,945 --> 00:18:39,745
I don't even have family anymore.

284
00:18:39,825 --> 00:18:41,425
What home is there to go back to?

285
00:18:41,505 --> 00:18:43,585
I'm sorry.

286
00:18:46,385 --> 00:18:48,865
All these years,
I've hated two holidays most.

287
00:18:50,065 --> 00:18:51,625
One is Mid-Autumn Festival,

288
00:18:52,465 --> 00:18:53,905
the other is New Year.

289
00:19:07,585 --> 00:19:08,465
Qiao.

290
00:19:11,385 --> 00:19:12,465
I'm actually

291
00:19:13,665 --> 00:19:18,145
here today to see you
because Sir asked me to.

292
00:19:20,025 --> 00:19:25,305
On New Year's Eve,
he wants to invite you over for dinner.

293
00:19:26,785 --> 00:19:28,505
I'm an outsider. It wouldn't be right.

294
00:19:28,585 --> 00:19:29,825
You guys go ahead and celebrate.

295
00:19:31,105 --> 00:19:32,825
Sir's exact words were,

296
00:19:33,345 --> 00:19:36,785
"Family should have
a reunion dinner together."

297
00:19:57,945 --> 00:19:59,625
If it doesn't work for you,

298
00:19:59,705 --> 00:20:01,185
I I can tell him

299
00:20:01,265 --> 00:20:02,625
-you're going out of town.
-It works for me!

300
00:20:06,065 --> 00:20:07,065
It really is.

301
00:20:08,745 --> 00:20:12,945
But on New Year's Eve,
I promised to take a part-time job.

302
00:20:13,025 --> 00:20:14,305
I might be a little late.

303
00:20:14,825 --> 00:20:16,145
But not too late.

304
00:20:16,665 --> 00:20:19,385
I will come as soon as I'm done.

305
00:20:22,065 --> 00:20:22,945
It's okay.

306
00:20:23,905 --> 00:20:25,025
I'll pick you up then.

307
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:51,105
BOWLS DRESS

308
00:20:56,185 --> 00:20:57,025
Kiddo,

309
00:20:57,985 --> 00:21:00,025
do you ever get this feeling?

310
00:21:00,105 --> 00:21:04,705
I keep feeling that this Bowls lead,
just like the blue heels,

311
00:21:06,105 --> 00:21:08,185
is a dead end. It goes nowhere.

312
00:21:08,265 --> 00:21:09,105
MAN WITH THREE BURN SCARS

313
00:21:11,025 --> 00:21:13,905
Yuanlongli's demolition is two weeks away.

314
00:21:14,505 --> 00:21:15,825
We need to hurry.

315
00:21:15,905 --> 00:21:18,665
Run the Tremaux algorithm
a few more times.

316
00:21:18,745 --> 00:21:19,745
Again?

317
00:21:20,545 --> 00:21:22,385
You keep running it
on the same few places.

318
00:21:22,985 --> 00:21:23,945
You're just going in circles.

319
00:21:24,785 --> 00:21:26,945
You might as well go to
the provincial capital with me tomorrow.

320
00:21:27,545 --> 00:21:30,505
Whether Bowls is a dead end,
we won't know until we go.

321
00:21:34,705 --> 00:21:36,385
Who messed with this?

322
00:21:36,465 --> 00:21:37,945
Who pulls something like this at night?

323
00:21:38,025 --> 00:21:40,265
Stay away from the window.

324
00:21:48,585 --> 00:21:50,585
Quick, go. Inside, inside.

325
00:22:04,865 --> 00:22:07,225
HOLDOUTS GROUP MESSAGE

326
00:22:13,185 --> 00:22:16,665
Who smashed my window? Was it Qian Dajun?

327
00:22:16,745 --> 00:22:17,585
Get out here!

328
00:22:17,665 --> 00:22:19,305
Is someone going crazy out there?

329
00:22:20,585 --> 00:22:23,665
DU MINGLIANG'S MOTHER
SHOE SELLER, LIU GUIFANG

330
00:22:43,025 --> 00:22:44,785
That Qian Dajun.

331
00:22:44,865 --> 00:22:47,985
Today he smashed a window,
tomorrow he'll break down the door.

332
00:22:49,785 --> 00:22:51,025
I can't go to the provincial capital.

333
00:22:51,105 --> 00:22:52,185
Someone has to stay home.

334
00:22:52,785 --> 00:22:53,865
You go and come back fast tomorrow.

335
00:22:54,585 --> 00:22:56,305
Dad, then promise me.

336
00:22:56,385 --> 00:22:57,865
No matter what happens,

337
00:22:57,945 --> 00:22:59,225
don't get physical.

338
00:22:59,305 --> 00:23:00,665
Call the police if you have to.

339
00:23:01,905 --> 00:23:05,185
With what little they can do,
why would I need the police?

340
00:23:07,065 --> 00:23:08,225
Dad.

341
00:23:15,385 --> 00:23:18,145
Fine. I promise.

342
00:23:18,225 --> 00:23:19,985
If I can argue, I won't fight.

343
00:23:20,665 --> 00:23:21,545
Promise me.

344
00:23:23,145 --> 00:23:25,025
I promise. I promise.

345
00:23:28,905 --> 00:23:31,225
Just don't bother with it today.
Get some sleep.

346
00:23:32,145 --> 00:23:34,025
When I'm back tomorrow, I'll help you.

347
00:23:40,265 --> 00:23:42,465
Be careful going downstairs.

348
00:24:00,865 --> 00:24:02,985
MAN WITH THREE BURN SCARS, BOWLS DRESS

349
00:24:03,065 --> 00:24:05,065
MOTHER OF DU MINGLIANG IN ROOM 1706
SHOEMAKER MR. LU

350
00:24:05,145 --> 00:24:07,425
SONG QINGSONG LIVED IN 1703
OFTEN BROUGHT BACK DIFFERENT GIRLS

351
00:24:07,505 --> 00:24:09,905
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

352
00:24:36,145 --> 00:24:36,985
Hello?

353
00:24:37,065 --> 00:24:39,625
Where are you?
The case briefing is about to start.

354
00:24:39,705 --> 00:24:41,345
-<i>I can't make it back today.</i>
-<i>What?</i>

355
00:24:41,425 --> 00:24:43,265
The case report,
I sent it to Captain Qu last night.

356
00:24:43,345 --> 00:24:45,425
Director Zou wants to praise
you by name at the briefing.

357
00:24:45,505 --> 00:24:48,105
-How can you not be there?
-I'm dealing with something urgent.

358
00:24:48,185 --> 00:24:49,625
I'll ask Captain Zhao
to file my leave request later.

359
00:24:50,305 --> 00:24:51,905
What are you busy with? Why so urgent?

360
00:24:54,785 --> 00:24:55,945
Captain Ran's last wish.

361
00:25:26,105 --> 00:25:27,865
Qiao. Come on.

362
00:25:27,945 --> 00:25:28,865
Have a seat inside.

363
00:25:39,825 --> 00:25:40,665
Uncle He.

364
00:25:41,825 --> 00:25:42,945
I need to apologize to you.

365
00:25:44,305 --> 00:25:47,745
About the demolition,
I did my best to persuade the boss.

366
00:25:47,825 --> 00:25:49,625
But he still sided with Qian Dajun.

367
00:25:49,705 --> 00:25:52,945
He's already given him
full control of the demolition.

368
00:25:53,025 --> 00:25:56,505
Yuanlongli
will likely be demolished early.

369
00:25:56,585 --> 00:25:57,665
I figured.

370
00:25:58,185 --> 00:26:00,145
They started playing dirty last night.

371
00:26:05,785 --> 00:26:06,625
I'm sorry, Uncle He.

372
00:26:06,705 --> 00:26:08,705
Why are you apologizing?

373
00:26:08,785 --> 00:26:09,785
It's not your fault.

374
00:26:10,945 --> 00:26:12,905
It's actually better that you're not
caught in the middle.

375
00:26:13,905 --> 00:26:15,585
Uncle He, please don't do anything rash.

376
00:26:15,665 --> 00:26:18,105
Qian Dajun might do something even worse.

377
00:26:18,185 --> 00:26:19,185
-Who knows what he'll do?
-Let him!

378
00:26:19,265 --> 00:26:20,985
I dare him to try!

379
00:26:21,745 --> 00:26:22,745
Uncle He.

380
00:26:22,825 --> 00:26:24,945
If anything happens to you,

381
00:26:25,025 --> 00:26:27,625
Ran won't be at peace in the afterlife.

382
00:26:28,225 --> 00:26:30,025
To see the Eye of the Vortex,

383
00:26:30,545 --> 00:26:32,905
you must become part
of the Eye of the Vortex.

384
00:26:35,465 --> 00:26:37,145
Those were Ran's words.

385
00:26:37,225 --> 00:26:38,465
None of you understood him.

386
00:26:39,585 --> 00:26:41,425
Only by making up for his regrets

387
00:26:41,505 --> 00:26:43,145
can he find peace.

388
00:26:50,545 --> 00:26:51,385
Uncle He.

389
00:26:51,465 --> 00:26:56,825
Ran gave this to me
just before New Year in 2003.

390
00:26:56,905 --> 00:27:00,065
I don't know
if it can help with what you're doing.

391
00:27:02,065 --> 00:27:03,545
Ran gave you this?

392
00:27:03,625 --> 00:27:04,465
What is it?

393
00:27:07,185 --> 00:27:08,465
I promised Ran

394
00:27:09,065 --> 00:27:10,785
I'd only open it

395
00:27:12,025 --> 00:27:13,065
when he said I could.

396
00:27:13,665 --> 00:27:16,785
But he never got to say it.

397
00:27:21,225 --> 00:27:22,825
SEAL

398
00:27:37,785 --> 00:27:39,465
LIANGLIANG COMPUTER SUPPLIES

399
00:27:43,145 --> 00:27:45,145
What are you doing? Building a bunker?

400
00:27:45,225 --> 00:27:48,025
Uncle He, the surface world has fallen.

401
00:27:48,105 --> 00:27:49,825
Next is our underground world.

402
00:27:49,905 --> 00:27:51,585
I have to arm myself.

403
00:27:52,985 --> 00:27:54,225
Open up and let me in first.

404
00:27:54,305 --> 00:27:55,225
Right.

405
00:28:08,065 --> 00:28:11,225
Uncle He, this drive was formatted.

406
00:28:11,305 --> 00:28:13,665
Everything inside was wiped.
It's all gone.

407
00:28:15,865 --> 00:28:16,785
What do we do?

408
00:28:17,345 --> 00:28:18,505
Can you recover it?

409
00:28:18,585 --> 00:28:20,825
This belonged to Officer Ran.
It's important.

410
00:28:21,385 --> 00:28:22,425
Three minutes.

411
00:28:27,625 --> 00:28:29,145
‎TOOLS, OPEN DISK

412
00:28:34,305 --> 00:28:35,145
Almost done.

413
00:28:36,785 --> 00:28:41,345
BOWLS INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.

414
00:28:44,505 --> 00:28:46,785
You must be Officer He, right?

415
00:28:47,345 --> 00:28:48,585
-Hello.
-Hello.

416
00:28:48,665 --> 00:28:51,945
BOWLS INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.

417
00:28:54,265 --> 00:28:55,305
WEIYANG STORE

418
00:28:55,385 --> 00:28:56,825
1996 to 2005.

419
00:28:57,825 --> 00:28:59,985
The Weiyang store's sales records
are all here.

420
00:29:02,745 --> 00:29:04,385
Officer He, take your time.

421
00:29:04,465 --> 00:29:05,745
I'll make you some tea.

422
00:29:05,825 --> 00:29:07,265
-Thank you.
-No problem.

423
00:29:12,265 --> 00:29:13,665
SALES LOG

424
00:29:15,745 --> 00:29:19,385
SUBJECT SEARCH: SUN ZHENGYONG

425
00:29:23,105 --> 00:29:24,265
DRY CLEANING GIFTCARD REFUND
FOR A SAME DRESS

426
00:29:30,585 --> 00:29:32,945
SUBJECT SEARCH: XU MENG

427
00:29:33,025 --> 00:29:34,465
DRY CLEANING LOG
CLIENT: XU MENG, BUYER: YAO XINCHENG

428
00:29:34,545 --> 00:29:35,385
Found it.

429
00:29:35,465 --> 00:29:39,345
According to the dry-cleaning record,
the buyer linked to this dress

430
00:29:39,425 --> 00:29:40,625
is Yao Xingcheng.

431
00:29:40,705 --> 00:29:44,465
He bought it on December 29, 1996,
at our store.

432
00:29:44,545 --> 00:29:46,705
Yao Xingcheng?

433
00:29:46,785 --> 00:29:47,705
BUYER YAO XINCHENG

434
00:29:47,785 --> 00:29:50,865
RETURN REASON: OTHER REASONS

435
00:29:50,945 --> 00:29:52,505
RETURN DATE: 1997/7/2

436
00:29:52,585 --> 00:29:53,705
That's strange.

437
00:29:54,385 --> 00:29:55,225
What is it?

438
00:29:55,825 --> 00:30:00,385
This Yao Xingcheng's information
only appears in the return record.

439
00:30:00,465 --> 00:30:03,145
His name isn't in the purchase record.

440
00:30:03,745 --> 00:30:07,625
He bought the dress
on December 29 in store.

441
00:30:07,705 --> 00:30:09,865
It was returned on July 2.

442
00:30:10,465 --> 00:30:12,065
The note says, "new returned for old".

443
00:30:13,385 --> 00:30:15,025
What does that mean?

444
00:30:15,945 --> 00:30:18,105
One moment. I'll ask the manager.

445
00:30:27,065 --> 00:30:27,985
Hello, Officer.

446
00:30:28,505 --> 00:30:29,745
I wrote that note.

447
00:30:29,825 --> 00:30:31,825
Back then, this customer
came back after over six months

448
00:30:31,905 --> 00:30:33,345
to make the return.

449
00:30:33,425 --> 00:30:35,705
But the tags and packaging
were all intact.

450
00:30:35,785 --> 00:30:37,905
So the counter canceled the order.

451
00:30:38,665 --> 00:30:40,465
What did the person
who returned it look like?

452
00:30:40,545 --> 00:30:41,945
Do you remember?

453
00:30:42,025 --> 00:30:43,065
I didn't handle the return.

454
00:30:43,145 --> 00:30:46,145
I only found the order while making
that day's report.

455
00:30:46,225 --> 00:30:49,345
This dress had its
button supplier changed in 1997.

456
00:30:49,425 --> 00:30:52,505
This customer bought the old version,
but returned the new one.

457
00:30:53,105 --> 00:30:54,185
I found it strange too.

458
00:30:54,265 --> 00:30:57,105
That's why I wrote that note.

459
00:30:58,665 --> 00:31:00,225
BOWLS FLAGSHIP STORE, SOLD BY SUSAN
COMMENT: WITH ONE DRY CLEANING GIFT CARD

460
00:31:00,905 --> 00:31:02,505
Officer.

461
00:31:02,585 --> 00:31:05,385
The returned dress wasn't bought here.

462
00:31:05,465 --> 00:31:06,745
It was bought
at the provincial flagship store.

463
00:31:07,945 --> 00:31:08,905
What do you mean?

464
00:31:09,705 --> 00:31:10,985
Here's the thing.

465
00:31:11,065 --> 00:31:14,985
This new dress was only distributed
on June 30, 1997.

466
00:31:15,065 --> 00:31:17,505
It arrived at the provincial store
on July 1.

467
00:31:17,585 --> 00:31:20,065
Our Weiyang store is farther away.
It arrived a week later.

468
00:31:20,585 --> 00:31:21,905
So you mean

469
00:31:21,985 --> 00:31:25,465
on July 2, your store wasn't selling
this new style yet?

470
00:31:25,545 --> 00:31:26,585
Right. Look.

471
00:31:26,665 --> 00:31:29,145
On July 2, at 10:05 a.m.,

472
00:31:29,225 --> 00:31:31,625
the provincial flagship store
had a sales record

473
00:31:31,705 --> 00:31:32,545
for the same dress.

474
00:31:32,625 --> 00:31:35,105
But in this record,
there's no customer name.

475
00:31:35,185 --> 00:31:37,705
The return at our store

476
00:31:38,425 --> 00:31:40,305
was at 4:20 p.m. that same day.

477
00:31:44,385 --> 00:31:45,625
Strange.

478
00:31:45,705 --> 00:31:47,265
Bought it in the provincial capital
that morning,

479
00:31:47,345 --> 00:31:48,785
then spent hours rushing to Weiyang,

480
00:31:48,865 --> 00:31:50,265
just to return the dress.

481
00:31:50,345 --> 00:31:51,865
Why go through all that?

482
00:31:57,905 --> 00:31:59,585
This return is strange.

483
00:31:59,665 --> 00:32:01,665
Jessica. Mark it clearly.

484
00:32:01,745 --> 00:32:04,385
In case the customer asks later,
we'll have an explanation.

485
00:32:04,465 --> 00:32:05,745
Yes, Manager.

486
00:32:10,745 --> 00:32:13,425
NOTE: NEW FOR OLD, BOUGHT IN CAPITAL
RETURNED IN WEIYANG. JESSICA

487
00:32:15,625 --> 00:32:18,665
This customer
bought it in the capital that morning,

488
00:32:18,745 --> 00:32:20,105
then returned it in Weiyang
that afternoon.

489
00:32:20,185 --> 00:32:22,145
And it canceled a record
from over six months ago.

490
00:32:22,945 --> 00:32:23,865
Why?

491
00:32:26,665 --> 00:32:28,625
Maybe they wanted to use the return

492
00:32:28,705 --> 00:32:31,065
to erase Yao Xingcheng's purchase record.

493
00:32:31,785 --> 00:32:35,185
Ma'am, can you help me contact
the Jessica who wrote this note?

494
00:32:35,265 --> 00:32:37,185
Jessica from the Weiyang store.

495
00:32:37,745 --> 00:32:39,905
I need to check HR's computer.

496
00:32:39,985 --> 00:32:40,985
One moment.

497
00:32:41,065 --> 00:32:42,745
-Thank you.
-No problem.

498
00:32:44,505 --> 00:32:47,225
Right. Can I make a copy of these files?

499
00:32:47,785 --> 00:32:49,505
Sure. You can copy them yourself.

500
00:33:06,665 --> 00:33:07,625
Uncle Ran,

501
00:33:09,745 --> 00:33:10,705
back then,

502
00:33:11,505 --> 00:33:12,825
did you find this too?

503
00:33:19,105 --> 00:33:20,785
SUBJECT SEARCH: RAN FANGXU

504
00:33:22,105 --> 00:33:23,305
SEARCH

505
00:33:23,385 --> 00:33:25,385
DATE: 2003/1/29, WEIYANG FLAGSHIP
CLIENT: RAN FANGXU

506
00:33:27,265 --> 00:33:28,865
SALESPERSON: JESSICA

507
00:33:31,065 --> 00:33:32,465
STORE: WEIYANG FLAGSHIP
CUSTOMER: RAN FANGXU

508
00:33:32,545 --> 00:33:33,385
<i>Thank you for your cooperation.</i>

509
00:33:34,225 --> 00:33:35,065
Of course.

510
00:33:35,145 --> 00:33:36,785
-I'll get going.
-Okay. Take care.

511
00:33:36,865 --> 00:33:37,745
See him out.

512
00:33:38,425 --> 00:33:39,585
Officer.

513
00:33:39,665 --> 00:33:40,785
New Year is coming soon.

514
00:33:40,865 --> 00:33:43,345
Would you like to see some clothes
and pick one for your family?

515
00:33:52,505 --> 00:33:53,545
Officer.

516
00:33:53,625 --> 00:33:55,625
You're handsome, and you have great taste.

517
00:33:55,705 --> 00:33:57,345
This just came in.
It's the Year of the Goat style.

518
00:33:57,425 --> 00:33:59,465
I can give you an extra discount.

519
00:34:10,264 --> 00:34:11,225
I recovered one file.

520
00:34:19,705 --> 00:34:20,545
Uncle He,

521
00:34:21,304 --> 00:34:23,625
